  The MiSTer framework by MiSTer-devel (Alexey Melnikov "Sorgelig" and contributors),
  https://github.com/MiSTer-devel/Template_MiSTer, commit 5dda37366d02b04b8448da7b322235c1831af811
  (2026-10-16). GPL-2.0-or-later and GPL-3.0-or-later by file (hps_io.sv: Till Harbaum 2014,
  Alexey Melnikov 2017-2026, GPL-3.0-or-later). Unchanged, except core/rtl/pll/pll_0002.v
  (96 MHz output). Included third-party parts of the template:
    - ascal.vhd: Avalon scaler by TEMLIB, 2018-2020, free to distribute and use.
    - spdif.v: SPDIF transmitter by Ultra-Embedded.com, 2012, GPL-2.0-or-later.
    - hq2x.sv: Ludvig Strigeus 2012-2013 and Sorgelig 2017-2018, GPL.
    - scandoubler.v, sd_card.sv: Till Harbaum 2015 / 2014, with MiSTer-devel changes.
  PLL files (core/rtl/pll.v, core/rtl/pll/, core/sys/pll*) are Intel/Altera megafunction
  output, used under Intel's licence for use with Altera devices.

Build tools (not shipped inside the core)
  Intel Quartus Prime Lite (the .rbf is built with it), Verilator and the OSS CAD Suite
  (testbenches), zig (Windows tools). Each has its own licence.

Games
  This repository contains no games. CHGame games (.CHG) and their data files (.DAT) belong
  to their authors.

  The release zip's games/CHGame/ folder and the optional downloader database hold three games
  by Jadflat, each under its own licence (the game's code, art and music MIT; the vendored
  CHGame library by Kevin Bates, Apache-2.0), with the licence beside it as LICENSE-<game>.txt:
    CHix      https://github.com/jadflat/CHix      (CHix.CHG)
    STARLIFT  https://github.com/jadflat/Starlift  (STARLIFT.CHG, STARLIFT.DAT)
    CHarth    https://github.com/jadflat/CHarth    (CHarth.CHG)
